lesson.body:
Income from house property is charged under sections 20 to 25 of the 2025 Act (sections 22 to 27 of the 1961 Act). The **annual value** of a building or land appurtenant to it is taxable in the hands of its **owner** if:

- the property consists of a building or land appurtenant;
- the assessee is the owner (legal or deemed);
- the property is not used for the owner's own business or profession (then it is business income).

**Deemed owner** includes: an individual who transfers a house to his spouse (not under an agreement to live apart) or minor child (not a married daughter) without adequate consideration; the holder of an impartible estate; a member allotted a house by a co-operative society; a person in possession under a part-performance contract; and a lessee for 12 years or more.

Composite rent for a building with furniture or services: if the letting is inseparable, it is taxed as business income or other sources; if separable, the building rent is house property income.
